# Commit Message Guidelines

Always use **gitmoji** (see [gitmoji reference](./gitmoji-reference.md)) at the start of every commit.

## Format

<emoji> <type>: <short, clear description>

## Rules

- Use **present tense** (“add”, not “added”)
- Keep the subject **≤ 72 characters**
- One commit = **one logical change**
- Be specific, avoid vague messages

## Common Examples

- ✨ feat: add user authentication flow
- 🐛 fix: resolve crash on empty input
- ♻️ refactor: simplify payment validation logic
- 📝 docs: update API usage examples
- 🚀 perf: improve query execution time
- ✅ test: add coverage for edge cases

## Bad Examples

- ❌ update stuff
- ❌ fixed bug
- ❌ changes

When unsure, pick the emoji that best represents the **intent** of the change.
